{"id": 26, "ts": 1780619904.5229864, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s detailed view of Candidate\u202fC\u2019s reliability and crew cooperation, and I also note Emily\u2019s confidence in Candidate\u202fB\u2019s operational reliability and stress resilience. However, we still lack a clear picture of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s ability to maintain calm under pressure and to work constructively with a crew. Sarah\u2019s input confirms that D \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately,\u201d indicating a baseline level of stress resilience, but the notes also flag him as \u201carrogant\u201d with \u201crelatively weak leadership skills,\u201d which raises concerns about his communication style and teamwork\u2014critical for long\u2011distance flights. Given that both leading candidates (C and B) have stronger evidence of calmness in crises (C keeps calm; B handles stress well) and better crew\u2011cooperation signals, I remain unconvinced that D can match them on these safety\u2011critical criteria. Therefore, I continue to favor Candidate\u202fC as the leading choice, while keeping an eye on the communication concerns that Sarah highlighted."}
